---
title: ForegroundPoolWatch · lost VM
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> Selecting
  Selecting --> Starting : Admit [runtime up]
  Starting --> Serving : Ready
  Starting --> Stopping : SettleFailed, UserStop
  Serving --> Stopping : UserStop
  Stopping --> Finishing : GraphStopped / disarm
  Finishing --> Settled : Finish
  Starting --> Exited : ExitOnLoss [lost, grace]
  Serving --> Exited : ExitOnLoss [lost]
  Stopping --> Exited : ExitOnLoss [lost, grace]
  Exited --> [*]
  Settled --> [*]

  note left of Starting
    Observe: pid gone or boot
    ended. Grace 10 s while
    starting or stopping.
  end note
  note right of Serving
    Grace 0 once ready.
  end note
  note right of Finishing
    Watch cancelled: a pool
    stop here is not a lost VM.
    INV NoExitAfterGraphStopped
  end note
  note right of Exited
    INV BoundedExit
    Names the lost VM and
    hack down --recover.
    Exit code 1.
  end note

  classDef live stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef wait stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef ok stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef fail stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef idle stroke-width:1.6px
  class Selecting idle
  class Starting,Stopping,Finishing wait
  class Serving live
